# Accepts VERP bounce addresses on the rbm subdomains as "deliverable".
# Without this, Postfix rejects them with 550 "User unknown in virtual mailbox table"
# (the subdomain is a virtual_mailbox_domain, but there is no 'bounces@' mailbox).
#
# The returned value only has to be NON-EMPTY for the RCPT to be accepted: the actual
# delivery is taken over by transport_maps (bounce_transport.regexp) and sent to the
# 'bounce-handler' pipe, so this "mailbox path" is never used.
#
# recipient_delimiter=+ -> matches both 'bounces@<sub>' and 'bounces+<verp>@<sub>'.
# Value = a non-empty constant (no capture is used; the delivery is taken over).
/^bounces(\+.*)?@rbm[0-9]+\.[^@]+$/   bounce-sink/
